<title>JAPAN: Key 182nd JGB yield falls to record low 2.285 pct.</title>
<headline>Key 182nd JGB yield falls to record low 2.285 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield of the benchmark cash 182nd 10-year Japanese government bond (JGB) fell to 2.285 percent in early Tokyo trade on Thursday, a record low.</p>
<p>The previous record low was 2.290 percent set on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Traders said investors, including some life insurers, were detected buying.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-9780</p>
</text>
